BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:POETRY at the BARN: Spoon River Anthology
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T150000
UID:865c81378e9c31e3ba215d4e318506a7@njpoetryevents.com
DESCRIPTION:Please join us in the Barn Gallery of Ringwood State Park for 
 a unique group reading from The Spoon River Anthology by Edgar Lee Masters
 . This presentation has been beautifully sequenced by George Lightcap. Cem
 etery "residents" in the fictional 19th century town of Spoon River return
  to confess\, extol\, educate\, complain\, or celebrate their lives. The h
 istoric Barn Gallery is a perfect backdrop for this free autumnal event an
 d everyone's welcome to attend! POETRY at the BARN is sponsored by Ringwoo
 d Manor Arts. Donations are always appreciated and can be made in person o
 r by visiting RingwoodManorArts.org For questions or more info please emai
 l Karen Lee Ramos at RMAApoetry@yahoo.com THEME: GROUP READING HOST: Karen
  Lee Ramos FEATURES: N/A PRICE: FREE - Donations Accepted - RingwoodManorA
 rts.org CONTACT: For questions or more info please email Karen Lee Ramos a
 t RMAApoetry@yahoo.com
LOCATION:Ringwood Manor Association of the Arts\, 1304 Sloatsburg Road\, R
 ingwood\, NJ\, 07456
URL:https://www.njpoetryevents.com/calendar/poetry-at-the-barn-spoon-river
 -anthology
X-SOURCE:NJ Poetry Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DANNY SIMMONS: DEF POETRY REUNION
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T200000
UID:4c27a1a3a8dd2b8e89e4354526061596@njpoetryevents.com
DESCRIPTION:From 2002–2007\, the spoken word revolution exploded on TV s
 creens around the world via&nbsp\; Russell Simmons presents Def Poetry . N
 early twenty years after the final episode aired on HBO\,&nbsp\; Def Poetr
 y Jam &nbsp\;alumni reunite to honor the man at the center of it all:&nbsp
 \; Abiodun Oyewole. The acclaimed poet is a founding member of The Last Po
 ets \, the groundbreaking Black nationalist poetry and music collective th
 at influenced generations of artists and laid the foundation for hip hop. 
 WBGO’s&nbsp\; Lezlie Harrison (host of&nbsp\; Come Sunday &nbsp\;and&nbs
 p\; Singers Unlimited ) emcees the evening. With performances and tributes
  by: Dr. Antoinette Ellis-Williams &nbsp\;is a multimedia interdisciplinar
 y abstract contemporary artist\, playwright\, scholar\, poet and author of
  Black Gardenias: A Collection of Poems\, Stories\, &amp\; Sayings from A 
 Woman’s Heart. D.Cross (Derick Cross) &nbsp\;is a multidimensional\, vis
 ual\, vocal poetic performance artist and arts educator. He served as a cu
 ltural hip hop ambassador for The U.S. State Department’s Next Level Pro
 gram. Kraal “Kayo” Charles &nbsp\;is a performer\, playwright and prod
 ucer. He was the youngest Grand Slam Champion at the legendary Nuyorican P
 oets Café in 1998. Bonafide Rojas &nbsp\;is a poet\, musician and the aut
 hor of&nbsp\; Excelsior \,&nbsp\; Notes On The Return To The Island \,&nbs
 p\; Renovatio \,&nbsp\; When The City Sleeps &nbsp\;and&nbsp\; Pelo Bueno 
 . He was awarded the 2023 Letras Boricuas Fellowship from The Mellon Found
 ation. Chris “Flowmentalz” Cook &nbsp\;is a prominent slam master\, sp
 oken word poet and non-profit organizer. He is widely known for hosting co
 mmunity open mics and poetry slams. With more special guests to be announc
 ed! THEME: HBO\,&nbsp\; Def Poetry Jam &nbsp\;Alumni Reunite HOST: NJPAC F
 EATURES: Dr. Antoinette Ellis-Williams * D.Cross (Derick Cross) * Kraal 
 “Kayo” Charles * Bonafide Rojas Chris “Flowmentalz” Cook * With mo
 re special guests to be announced! PRICE: Tickets $34.40 - https://www.tic
 ketmaster.com/event/000064BC8BDA8206 CONTACT: 1.888.696.5722 / IG - @njpac
  / FB - NJPAC
LOCATION:NJPAC (Victoria Theater Lizzie &amp\; Jonathan Tisch Stage)\, 1 C
 enter Street\, Newark\, NJ\, 07102
URL:https://www.njpoetryevents.com/calendar/danny-simmons-def-poetry-reuni
 on
X-SOURCE:NJ Poetry Events
END:VEVENT
